-- examples/checks/agg-join-delta-first-steps.rofl — A STEPS WALL CUTS WHERE THE WRITTEN ORDER CUTS.
--
-- p(Q, Y) :- h(X, Z), l(X, Y), trig(Y, Z, Q) over 40 + 40 + 10 rows. Under a budget that runs
-- out inside the firing, which conclusions came before the cut depends on the order the
-- solutions are concluded in. Two worlds read this file under the same budget: one in
-- written order, as every firing is under a wall a caller set (agg_breaks
-- `delta_first_walls`), one opted into the plans (check_opt delta_first), where a firing
-- whose conclusions could reach the wall is solved again in written order (agg_breaks
-- `delta_first_cut_unchecked`). Both cut where the TypeScript engine cuts.
-- expect-row: p[main](q,y1) tick
-- expect-row: p[main](q,y6) tick
-- expect-no-row: p[main](q,y2) tick
-- expect-no-row: p[main](q,y5) tick
edb(h). edb(l). edb(trig).
p(Q, Y) :- h(X, Z), l(X, Y), trig(Y, Z, Q).
